## Verdict (12 October 2026)

- 0.99 is reachable on all four maps with additive splats and short oriented segments, and with far fewer elements AND bytes than the 2.5 million polygons (485 MB) per region pass. (12 October 2026)
- But only Bump is genuinely compact (about 181 000 to 204 000 points, 4 to 5 percent of the pixel count). For Cavity, Specular and NormalR, 0.99 needs 1.0 to 1.75 million elements, i.e. 24 to 42 percent of the 4.19 million pixels, and the dominant atom is a sigma 0.35 px splat, which is a single pixel. Honestly stated: for those maps the element set is a sparse re-encoding of the image grain, close to storing the image (Specular: estimated packed size about 0.9 of the lossless image; Cavity about 0.5). (12 October 2026)
- Curves (oriented segments) help only modestly: minus 6 to 18 percent elements at 0.99. The crack lines are a small share of the residual; the bulk is a pixel-scale grain spread over the whole surface (see `data/Cavity_crop_ref_cur_resid.png`, right panel). (12 October 2026)

## Method (12 October 2026)

- Residual E = reference minus current result. Greedy matching pursuit by FFT correlation with wrap (tileable): each iteration takes local maxima (3x3) of the best energy gain over the dictionary, keeps the top max(20 000, 15 percent) of them, subtracts amplitude x kernel, repeats until Pearson >= 0.995. Then a least-squares amplitude refit (25 conjugate-gradient iterations, positions fixed) at checkpoints, plus an 8-bit amplitude quantisation check. (12 October 2026)
- Dictionary "iso": isotropic additive Gaussian splats, sigma 0.35, 0.7, 1.2, 2.0, 3.2 px, peak = amplitude. Dictionary "iso+seg": iso plus oriented segments (Gaussian along 2.0 px, about 7 px long; across 0.5 or 0.9 px; 8 orientations), the building block of a crack curve. (12 October 2026)
- Scripts: `workflow_cavity/scripts/AtomPursuit.py` (final method), `SplatPursuit.py` (first separable version, 4 sigmas starting at 0.6, kept because its atoms are saved and used for byte counts), `ResidualStats.py`, `AtomBytes.py`, `Summarize.py`. Data: `workflow_cavity/data/summary.json`, `*_iso*_atoms.json`, `residual_stats.json`, `atom_bytes.json`. (12 October 2026)

